From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:30:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_input: follow configuration changes

The Kernarium host plugs and unplugs a hardware keyboard, mouse and
pointer while the guest runs, as devices that always exist and whose
configuration changes. The driver read the device once at probe and had
no config_changed, so a plug could never reach it.

Read the identity, every event bitmap and the range of every absolute
axis into one configuration, register the input device from it when the
device reports at least one event type, and have none otherwise. A
configuration change schedules a work item that reads everything again,
every time, since nothing ties the reads of one change together. When
the device reports no event type the input device is unregistered, which
releases its keys in the input core; when anything differs from what was
registered, the input device is registered again. Event delivery uses
RCU so that a delivery in progress never sees an input device go.

Post the event buffers at probe even when there is no input device: the
host answers a device as unplugged until its driver has done so, so a
driver that waited for the plug would never see one.

Answer with the private registration notice of virtio_input_uml.h on the
status queue: at probe when it registers an input device, on every
configuration change that leaves one registered (also one that finds it
registered already), and with value 0 for an unregistration. The header
is the host's copy, synchronized by the project's sync-protocol tool. A
resume schedules the same work, because the device was reset and may
have changed meanwhile.

A device that reports its events at probe registers as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
